  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.3.0: distribution release. Targets net8.0, net9.0, net10.0 and net11.0\n            (C# 15), adds the RVZSharp.Cli .NET tool package and WinGet distribution, and\n            fixes literal surrounding quotes in CLI path arguments. Dependency updates\n            include Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk 18.12.0 (CVE-2026-105544 fix). Public API stays\n            compatible with 1.0.0.\n            1.2.0: security and robustness release. CLI convert now defaults to RVZ with\n            Dolphin-compatible block/compression defaults, hostile-input parsing is bounded\n            (WIA/TGC/GCZ/NFS/FST, table and stream arithmetic), TGC extraction handles\n            unsigned 32-bit sizes, and warning-or-higher logs are forwarded to the\n            bug-report API with the required payload sections. Adds CodeQL, dependency\n            review, cross-platform CI and DocFX API docs. Public API stays compatible with\n            1.0.0. 613 library tests per framework and 97 CLI tests.\n            1.1.1: one-shot Zstd chunk compression (level 22 no longer reserves ~128 MiB\n            per parallel worker; output verified byte-identical in Dolphin's dolphin-tool,\n            including a full codec interop matrix) and no empty symbols package (assemblies\n            carry embedded PDBs). Public API stays compatible with 1.0.0.\n            1.1.0: legacy writers (CisoWriter, WbfsWriter, TgcWriter), the DiscVerifier Wii\n            hash-tree/TMD/H3 verifier, thread-safe ReadAt with an LRU cache, the async API,\n            split plain ISO, DiscInfo, BlobStream and scrub options; CLI --json output, -\n            stdin/stdout piping and shell completions; CI with API-compat validation and an\n            embedded SPDX SBOM. Fixes: partition keys are common-key decrypted from the ticket\n            (verify/extract work on real encrypted discs), extract TMD/cert/H3 offsets, WBFS\n            header size/disc-header copy, convert --json stdout hygiene, Ctrl+C exit 130 and\n            monotonic writer progress. Public API stays compatible with 1.0.0.",
